  "title": "Qin unification of China",
  "summary": "Between 230 and 221 BCE the state of Qin under King Ying Zheng conquered Han, Zhao, Wei, Chu, Yan and finally Qi. In 221 BCE he proclaimed himself Shi Huangdi, first emperor, and founded the Qin dynasty, which centralised power and standardised weights, measures, coinage and writing.",
